        "content": "Review task: Greeting CLI\n\nCreate `hello.py`: when run it prints exactly `Hello, Eidolon!`. Create `test_hello.py` with one pytest test that runs hello.py with `sys.executable` via subprocess and asserts the output. Run the tests with run_tests until they pass.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- hello.py prints exactly `Hello, Eidolon!` followed by a newline\n- test_hello.py exists and `python -m pytest -q` passes in the workspace\n- standard library only\n\nSubmitted files (also present in the workspace):\n--- hello.py ---\n\"\"\"Print a greeting for Eidolon.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    print(\"Hello, Eidolon!\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n--- test_hello.py ---\n\"\"\"Test that hello.py prints the expected greeting.\"\"\"\n\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHELLO = Path(__file__).resolve().parent / \"hello.py\"\n\n\ndef test_hello_output():\n    result = subprocess.run(\n        [sys.executable, str(HELLO)],\n        capture_output=True,\n        text=True,\n    )\n    assert result.returncode == 0\n    assert result.stdout == \"Hello, Eidolon!\\n\"\n\n\nCheck the work against the criteria (run the tests with run_tests if any), then answer with the JSON verdict only.",
